<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferenc Nagy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1903">1903</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferenc Nagy was a leader of the Independent Smallholders' Party who served as Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from February 1946 to May 1947, during the short-lived Second Hungarian Republic. The Communists, backed by the Soviet occupation, broke up his party through arrests and accusations of conspiracy. While on holiday in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> he was forced to resign, and he spent the rest of his life in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferenc-nagy.jpg" alt="Ferenc Nagy" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arlen (MTI photo) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nagy_Ferenc-MTI_1946.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
